2026-10-19 V4L2 on the Pi 4: CLOSED as not worth it (measured with dcheck libcef + timers). With patch 0001 (NV12 first + CAPTURE SetFormat) the V4L2 decoder runs, but Chromium
must convert NV12 -> AR24 on the CPU with LibYUV (GBM has no NV12 on V3D/X11; the GL image processor only does NV12->NV12): 60-120 ms per 1080p frame because the dmabuf mappings are uncached
(read 2 MB = 5-14 ms). A cached bounce patch (experimental-libyuv-cached-bounce.patch) gets 33-55 ms: still ~15 fps at 1080p, 55% dropped, 146% CPU; software FFmpeg decode is better (1080p ~15% dropped, 52% CPU).
`AcceleratedVideoDecoder` stays OUT of the `pi` profile, shipped arm64 deb unchanged. A second video in one browser session also hung the probe. Only a different output path (no CPU conversion) would change this.
- x64 CEF 147 (+codecs) verified 2026-10-18 on the VM (GTX 1060 passthrough) and venus (read-only): canPlayType probably for avc1/mp4a/vp8/vp9/av01, no for hevc/ac3/eac3/theora; H.264 720p/1080p+AAC play with FFmpegVideoDecoder/FFmpegAudioDecoder, 0 dropped frames; HEVC fails (DEMUXER_ERROR_NO_SUPPORTED_STREAMS). videoDecoding is empty on both (no VA-API): VM = NVIDIA (excluded upstream), venus = llvmpipe because 2026.10.22 lacks the i915 firmware (iHD init fails; fixed in 2026.10.24, re-test then).
