DESIGN CALL: step 3 does not just scaffold tests against not-yet-written code.
The three parsers (ddc.py), the EDID decoder + xrandr-EDID-property extractor
+ RandR/DRM name normaliser (identity.py) and the auto/explicit mechanism
priority resolution (mechanism.py) are ALL pure - no subprocess, no sysfs
reads, no PySide6/cefpython - so they were implemented for real now, with real
pytest coverage, rather than left as skeletons. Step 4 (hardware layer) adds
the impure counterparts on TOP of these already-tested functions: subprocess
wrapping with timeouts, asyncio.to_thread, per-bus/per-device locks, sysfs/
xrandr output enumeration, the capability-cache persistence model, and the
async facade (probe(), apply_power/input/volume/mute()) - it should not need
to touch ddc.py/identity.py/mechanism.py's existing functions, only add to the
package around them. Confirmed importable with zero PySide6/cefpython pulled
in (36 new modules on import, none of them Qt/CEF).

REAL GOTCHA FOUND WRITING THIS: manager/utils/models/command_line.py's
CommandLineArgs is a pydantic_settings BaseSettings with cli_parse_args=True,
so merely IMPORTING it parses sys.argv - and under pytest that argv is
pytest's own (test paths, -v, ...), which argparse rejects, INTERNALERROR-ing
the whole run before a single test executes. Every chain through manager/api
or manager/utils/models eventually imports it (cron.py -> wsmanager.py ->
models.remote -> models.command_line is the one hit here). Fixed in
manager/tests/conftest.py by sanitising sys.argv to argv[:1] before any test
module's own imports run - must be conftest.py specifically, since it loads
first. Recorded in CLAUDE.md.

SECOND FINDING, corrects something written in the previous session's entry
below and in SCREEN-CONTROL-PLAN.md/CLAUDE.md (both already amended): `xrandr
--props`'s EDID property, promoted to the primary RandR->monitor-identity
route after it worked on unitotem-test, does NOT work on this project's own
dev host - zero EDID properties on three connected outputs. Root cause found,
not left as a mystery: the dev host's `:0` is XWayland (`ps` confirms
`/usr/bin/Xwayland :0 ...`), whose RandR is an emulation layer over Wayland's
own output protocol (`xrandr --props` shows `RANDR Emulation: 1` there, absent
from the VM's capture) and never forwards EDID. Irrelevant to the kiosk, which
never runs Wayland/XWayland - but the code has to treat "no EDID property
returned" as a legitimate, handled outcome (fall back to
/sys/class/drm/<conn>/edid if present, else report the mechanism unavailable),
not as a bug, since testing this against a developer's own desktop hits this
path routinely. Both real captures (the working VM one and the empty XWayland
one) are test fixtures now.

Coverage: 64 tests, all passing (`.venv/bin/pytest manager/tests/`) - 3
genuine test-writing bugs of my own caught and fixed by actually running the
suite rather than hand-deriving expected values (a getvcp fixture whose real
D6 value had drifted between two captures in the same session - x01 to x04,
a real monitor power-state change while the node ran the codec agent's
headless stopgap, not a capture error; and a parse_version test table that
had (major, patch) where the implementation - correctly - returns
(major, minor)).

Two things step 3 explicitly did NOT do, staying inside its own scope: no
setvcp/write path (still pending explicit go-ahead, per the step-1/hardware
session below), and no CEC subprocess wrapping (still no CEC-capable hardware
anywhere this has been tested).

NEXT: step 4 (hardware layer: subprocess-calling ddc.py/identity.py additions,
cec.py, xorg.py, the async facade in __init__.py, and the persistence model).

